<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamunanagar district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamunanagar is a district in the north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haryana">Haryana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the west bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna River</a>, formed in 1989 from part of Ambala district. Its headquarters, the city of Yamunanagar with the adjoining town of Jagadhri, is an industrial centre known for plywood, paper and metal goods. The district includes the former lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cis-sutlej-states">Cis-Sutlej states</a> of Buria and Kalsia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yamunanagar-district.jpg" alt="Yamunanagar district" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pankajkukreti03 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Front_view_of_Ashok_Satambh_Park_at_topra_kalan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
